Step 1: Create the child component
In the VS Code terminal, run:
ng generate component child


This creates a separate folder for the child component.
Step 2: Write the code in each file
Your project might use either newer filenames (app.ts) or older filenames (app.component.ts). I'll show the code for the newer format first.
File 1: src/app/child/child.ts

Copy the entire code into this file:
import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-child',
  standalone: true,
  templateUrl: './child.html'
})
export class Child {
  @Input() student = {
    name: '',
    roll: 0,
    course: ''
  };
}


 Copy TypeScript code
File 2: src/app/child/child.html

Copy the entire code into this file:
<h2>Student Details</h2>
<p>Name: {{ student.name }}</p>
<p>Roll No: {{ student.roll }}</p>
<p>Course: {{ student.course }}</p>


 Copy HTML code
File 3: src/app/app.ts

Copy the entire code into this file:
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { Child } from './child/child';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [Child],
  templateUrl: './app.html'
})
export class App {
  student = {
    name: 'Vedant',
    roll: 101,
    course: 'Computer Science'
  };
}


